   "title": "Write ligatures as letters, so that a quote search finds the words",
   "note": "pdf_pages.py takes the first pdftotext on PATH, which in Git Bash is Git's Xpdf 4.00. Its text keeps typographic ligatures: the audit counted 65 fi and 4 fl ligatures in the text of one validation paper, so a search of paper.txt for \"specific\" misses the word. Step 9 of the skill and the calibration checklist rest on searching paper.txt for every quote and for \"the paper does not state\". Only the five Latin ligatures are replaced. A general Unicode normalization would also turn a superscript 2 into a 2, which changes numbers.",
